                "text": "Recorded by @dude-spec-lead at first definition and revised after independent review rejection (`define automatic-unchanged-intent-redefinition` -> `.dude/specs/015-automatic-unchanged-intent-redefinition/spec.md`). Scope and user intent are unchanged, and all nine user answers remain byte-unchanged above and compile as follows:\n\n- Q1: `plan.md` and `tasks.md` may change. `spec.md` may change only for the three settled outcome-equivalent correction classes. Route may change; promised outcome may not.\n- Q2: Eligibility requires a causally traced deterministic contradiction/impossible gate or current Feature 009 no-alternative evidence. A provable contradiction requires no pointless retry.\n- Q3: Every old obligation maps completely to an equal-or-stronger successor; user sections remain byte-identical; every check is retained or replaced by an invariant-equivalent successor. Deterministic validation proves closed shape, anchors, references, and completeness only. One independent semantic reviewer judges equal-or-stronger meaning and task-scope, acceptance-obligation, decomposition-basis, invariant, and successor-check equivalence against the coordinator-composed exact final bytes and mappings.\n- Q4: The intended invariant remains binding. A proven-defective literal may be replaced only with preserved trigger evidence and a reviewed successor check.\n- Q5: Structural protection validates the complete coordinator-composed four-path proposal before review. After exact-proposal approval and apply, one synchronous rollback callback rereads and reparses all four paths, compares exact bytes and identities, revalidates approval identity, and runs fresh lint plus required verification; any failure throws and restores all four paths or reports distinct incomplete rollback.\n- Q6: State survives only a one-to-one task whose scope and acceptance obligations the exact-proposal reviewer finds unchanged. Changed, split, and merged work reopens. The narrow `dropped-defective` exception permits automatic archival of a non-open task only in explicit autonomous Lightweight recovery under the complete evidence, successor, review, open-state, history, and archive conditions above; all other non-open drops still pause for user confirmation. Coordinator authority is unchanged.\n- Q7: Initial scope is Lightweight-only; tracked recovery still refuses before writes.\n- Q8: The coordinator composes exact final bytes before one semantic review and applies only that approved proposal. Successful synchronous post-apply identity, lint, and verification checks require no second semantic review. The coordinator-owned optional lane snapshot must then refresh through its existing all-or-restored boundary before resume and is not a fifth definition path. Ambiguity or normative change stops for the user.\n- Q9: Another redefinition requires new distinguishing evidence under Feature 009, the sole repeat/no-progress authority. Hashes identify exact proposals but never prove semantic decomposition equivalence; the reviewer supplies proposal-bound semantic evidence, and Feature 009 decides whether the same blocker or equivalent decomposition lacks distinguishing evidence and routes to existing `no-progress-verified`. Budgets remain backstops.\n\nThe lean package contains only `spec.md`, `plan.md`, and `tasks.md`. It compiles zero active ObjectiveRegistry regions. No supporting artifact applies, and no new project-wide guardrail candidate emerged beyond the ratified deterministic and smallest-design rules.",
