            "ideaPath": ".dude/ideas/057-dude-canvas-needs-you.md",
            "slug": "dude-canvas-needs-you",
            "specPath": ".dude/specs/057-dude-canvas-needs-you/spec.md",
            "title": "Dude Canvas Needs You",
            "intent": {
              "text": "User request, with transcription cleanup:\n\n> Review the session and identify use cases, scenarios, or situations that happened but might not be covered by the functionality we plan to implement. My point is: when did the agent need me, the user, and how does that fit into Dude? When we implement Dude Canvas Needs You, I want us to capture those scenarios. With those discoveries and your existing knowledge, go ahead and capture and brainstorm the feature.\n\nThe user subsequently permitted reviewing as many useful sessions as needed. The coordinator understood this as permission for wider sampling and reviewed other-session reports already in this project.\n\nProposed outcome: see and understand outstanding requests for my input, decision, consent, manual action, or host observation, with the right context and handoff.\n\nThe accepted broader Canvas vision is interactive, over the same active agent session. Earlier question-only I2 plus copied commands is a historical baseline being reconsidered. The Spec Lead recommends read-only orientation with response handoff first, separating display coverage from execution. This is not a user-ratified boundary.\n\nClarification (Spec Lead interpretat",
              "truncated": true,
              "source": {
                "path": ".dude/ideas/057-dude-canvas-needs-you.md",
                "section": "Idea"
              }
            },
            "dispositions": [
              {
                "text": "The revised requirements gate is satisfied for planning without changing any user answer. Q4 is reflected in the staged package. Save as idea continues to reuse blank-slate capture and discoverability: at use time, the user explicitly selects intent to capture through brainstorm. Ordinary Defer never auto-creates an idea or claims durable retention. Source-backed deferred matters keep their existing owner/source without a duplicate ledger. An unfiled matter without acknowledged capture remains visibly unsaved or uncertain; losing session context cannot become successful deferral. Save selected intent, not request queues, claim tokens, stale permissions, or sensitive payloads by default. Capture requires owner acknowledgment and canonical reread and grants neither definition nor execution authority. This is a definition-owner interpretation, not a new user answer or advance capture permission.\n\nThe plan retains one bounded extension publication/reply handoff for intake, definition/design, and coordinator human-stop callers. Pending responses return through the requesting tool; the current owner applies or refuses them and acknowledges with fresh evidence. Annotation delivery adds report text and actual PNG to that same waiting tool, not a standalone Sharpie send. Idle idea capture uses the joined session only after a blocking tool yields. Projection supplies discovery and cannot turn blank answers or historical activity into requests.\n\nThe supplied read-only architecture findings identify an HTML subset needing no new npm dependency, but image capture still requires an available Chromium-family executable. The expanded host-proof task must establish actual capture and installed text/image receipt before heavy UI work. No automatic browser installation, optional-screenshot substitute, or narrowed consumer promise is authorized. If the established install/build-free target cannot be met with available capability, return the concrete material scope choice before dependent work. This remains unproved, not a newly invented user answer.\n\nOnly the core trio is defined. Design stays `exploring`; `.dude/specs/057-dude-canvas-needs-you/design/needs-you-workspace.html` is the exact future primary preview, not an existing or approved mock. Seven proposed task units cover expanded host proof, mock approval, unchanged discovery, typed handoff, scoped annotation adoption, UI integration, and acceptance/packaging. Reconciliation retains one key, replaces five changed meanings with fresh keys, and adds one adapter unit; coordinator-owned task state and reconciliation remain unapplied. No archive, discovered-work, or execution history is introduced. No new guardrails, Ship authority, implementation, or execution permission is created.",
                "truncated": false,
                "source": {
                  "path": ".dude/ideas/057-dude-canvas-needs-you.md",
                  "section": "Definition Disposition"
                },
                "attribution": "managed-source"
              }
            ],
